prison|PASS: A converted prison museum illustrates the institution noun without inventing detention law. Especially qualifies punishment after a court decision; article omission is limited to the imprisonment construction.
toddler|PASS: Recently walking is a developmental boundary, not a universal numerical age. The example contains no safety recommendation; low steps and holding the father's hand align naturally in Vietnamese.
wedding|PASS: Event and associated celebration are distinguished from the continuing marriage relationship. The garden location is fictional and translated faithfully; the noun is countable rather than an abstract institution.
deforestation|REVIEW: The proposal describes forest removal rather than pruning, but the broad draft boundary needs comparison with formal land-use definitions. The map example makes no unsupported causal or statistical claim.
everything|REVIEW: Singular agreement and context-limited totality are explicit. The repair-bag translation preserves all needed things rather than every object in existence; full pronoun identity and pragmatic coverage remain unresolved.
